    },
    {
      "section": "7.3",
      "label": "(11)",
      "text": "The PCA pump must ﬁlter power interference 141 from mains.",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "7.4",
      "label": "(1)",
      "text": "The PCA pump shall perform a power-on self-test 142 (POST) to assure system integrity after being turned on, yet before any infusion begins. Failure of POST shall raise a POST alarm , stop pump, record it in the Fault Log, and display the reason for failure on the user interface. (EC4 §4.2.4)",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "7.4",
      "label": "(2)",
      "text": "The PCA pump shall perform periodic self-tests 143 to assure system integrity during long periods of use. Failure of a self-test shall raise a self-test alarm , stop pump, record it in the Fault Log, and display the reason for failure on the user interface. (EC22c §4.2.22)",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "7.4",
      "label": "(3)",
      "text": "The PCA pump shall have continuous fault-detection144 and masking. Hardware monitors of thread heartbeat, memory error correction codes are examples. (EC22d §4.2.22)",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "7.4",
      "label": "(4)",
      "text": "Occurrence of unavoidable single-event upsets 145 caused by cosmic-ray-induced high- and thermal-energy neutrons must be either masked, or detected to fail-stop. (EC22d §4.2.22)",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "7.4",
      "label": "(5)",
      "text": "Successfully masked faults 146 shall be recorded in the Fault Log, but not raise an alarm. (EC22e §4.2.22)",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "7.4",
      "label": "(6)",
      "text": "All unmasked hardware detected faults147 shall raise a fault alarm, stop pump, record it in the Fault Log, and display the reason for fault on the user interface. (EC22 §4.2.22)",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "7.4",
      "label": "(7)",
      "text": "Hardware faults that prevent operation of the Control Panel shall illuminate a hardware fault indicator148 (light-emitting diode). (EC22f §4.2.22)",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "7.5",
      "label": "(1)",
      "text": "Because the drugs used for analgesia are often narcotic, requiring Drug Enforcement Agency (DEA) tracking if used in the United States, the drug reservoir and means to change prescriptions during infusion must be inhibited with a locked, tamper-resistant door149.",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "7.5",
      "label": "(2)",
      "text": "Before infusion, the door must be closed and locked. 150 (UC1.10 §4.1.1)",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "7.5",
      "label": "(3)",
      "text": "Hospital procedures must endow the attending clinician access to the door key 151, yet prevent other persons’ access. Key-handling processes are beyond the scope of these requirements, but much depends on the attending clinician: it’s the right drug, in the right patient, with the right prescription from a physician authorized to prescribe narcotics for those suﬀering great pain.",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "section": "7.5",
      "label": "(4)",
      "text": "The PCA pump case 152 must be at least diﬃcult to breech as its tamper-resistant door. Breaking the case shall not be easier to access the drug reservoir than breeching the door.",
      "id": null
    }
